module gunbc.floor_cost_debt_verdict_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the cost-debt VERDICT wall: a floor_cost_debt row the change admits or
// restores must stand over a passing claim. The modeled authority is
// v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_verdict; the declarations below are its seed-side reader and mirror at
// the required floor's diff and terminal boundaries, not a second policy.
data floor_cost_debt_verdict_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_admitted_identities", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_verdict_refusals", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_comparison_base_commit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_roster_in_tree", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_base_tree_extract", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_scratch_dir", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "changed_with_cost_debt_admissions", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_admitted_by_fold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "merge_cost_debt_admissions", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_verdict_wall", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "cost_debt_roster_head_closure", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "record_cost_debt_verdict", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST IS STILL NEEDED: the required floor plans and executes its claims in the seed, and the two populations this wall joins -- the diff's changed identities and the terminal ledger -- never leave v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner run_required_floor. Every decision is the .dag's: which rows a change admits is v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_verdict cost_debt_admitted_identities_against_base (the head roster minus the base roster's evaluated result), and whether an owed row stands is cost_debt_verdict_cause_for_reading. The seed items do only what the fold cannot from that loop: resolve the comparison commit with the merge-base arm applied (cost_debt_comparison_base_commit), materialize the source roots at that commit (cost_debt_base_tree_extract into cost_debt_scratch_dir) and evaluate the base roster there (cost_debt_roster_in_tree), hand the result to the fold (cost_debt_admitted_by_fold, read by cost_debt_admitted_identities), merge the admitted rows into the changed set the floor plans from (changed_with_cost_debt_admissions, merge_cost_debt_admissions), and hand each owed identity's terminal reading to the fold (cost_debt_verdict_refusals, cost_debt_verdict_wall), and write the refusals onto the outcome (record_cost_debt_verdict). No verdict table, no admission rule and no cause wording lives in Rust (reviews 76257, 76273).\n\nWHAT IT REPAIRS: a cost row hid a semantic red. Two v2.test.claim.body_lowering.single_arm_match identities regressed at gunbc#13056 while rostered in floor_cost_debt_censored_chunk_03, and every required lane stayed green (gunbc#13327). Before this, a row was declined at build on the very change that added it, so nothing ever established that the claim it withholds passes.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits work serving the v2 self-host program; the required floor guards it, and this closes a hole through which a v2 compiler regression went unread. It adds no language behavior, no seed feature, no emitted surface and no flag: nothing an author writes can stand the wall down.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +12, the declarations above. The admission is asked whenever the diff touches a file the head roster's closure loads (cost_debt_roster_head_closure), and the wall's refusals reach the outcome through record_cost_debt_verdict, which run_required_floor and the integration control both call. required_floor_outcome_is_clean MOVED from the claim_executor binary into v1_compiler.cli_run unchanged, so it is a relocation rather than a new item.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete the seed declarations when the self-emitted claim executor builds the required floor's claim roster and terminal ledger and calls v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_verdict cost_debt_admitted_identities_against_base (with the base roster evaluated at the comparison commit) and cost_debt_verdict_cause_for_reading directly, so no hand-written reader carries the base tree, the changed set or the terminal readings across. NOT retired by the cost-debt roster reaching zero: an empty roster still needs its next admission judged.",
  current_boundary: "v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_verdict cost_debt_admitted_identities_against_base -> v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner cost_debt_admitted_identities -> v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner changed_with_cost_debt_admissions -> v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner run_required_floor -> v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner cost_debt_verdict_wall -> v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_verdict cost_debt_verdict_cause_for_reading -> v1_compiler.cli_run RequiredFloorOutcome cost_debt_verdict_refused"
}
